      "text": "Certificate issuer signature: ecdsa-with-SHA256 (classical)\nLeaf certificate subject='CN=github.com' was issued using ecdsa-with-SHA256 as the CA/issuer signature over the certificate. This is a classical (non-post-quantum) signature algorithm. This describes the certificate's chain-of-trust signature only \u2014 it is NOT the live TLS handshake's authentication signature (CertificateVerify), which uses the leaf's own key and can use a different algorithm (issue #226)."
